{"questions":[{"question_id":"1ky7d0ve2","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"chemical-reactions-for-aldehydes-and-ketones","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"consider-all-possible-isomeric-ketones-including-stereoisome-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-avqcrgfvct7hu2iy","content":"Consider all possible isomeric ketones including stereoisomers of MW = 100. All these isomers are independently reacted with NaBH<sub>4</sub> (Note : stereoisomers are also reacted separately). The total number of ketones that give a racemic product(s) is/are","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"Molecular weight of the ketone is 100. So, molecular formula = C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>12</sub>O.\nThe possible number of ketones with molecular formula C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>12</sub>O is six. Out of these, the total number of ketones that give a racemic product(s) on reaction with NaBH<sub>4</sub> is 5. The structure with chiral carbon will not give racemic product on reduction. <br>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1axn5w5/a1e04f09-4cca-4084-acd0-f7bd2272d408/3d415c50-aeb5-11ec-a750-090dba8947a4/file-1l1axn5w6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1axn5w5/a1e04f09-4cca-4084-acd0-f7bd2272d408/3d415c50-aeb5-11ec-a750-090dba8947a4/file-1l1axn5w6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 61 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1axn5w5/a1e04f09-4cca-4084-acd0-f7bd2272d408/3d415c50-aeb5-11ec-a750-090dba8947a4/file-1l1axn5w6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1axn5w5/a1e04f09-4cca-4084-acd